### Current Working Directory

The filesystem backend is rooted at `/` which maps to your project workspace on disk.
All file operations use virtual paths starting with `/` (e.g., `/src/main.py`).

### File System and Paths

**IMPORTANT - Path Handling:**
- All file paths must be absolute virtual paths (e.g., `/file.txt` or `/src/main.py`)
- The root directory `/` maps to your project workspace
- Example: To create a file in your project, use `/research_project/file.md`
- Never use relative paths - always construct full absolute paths starting with `/`
- **Never use Windows-style paths** (e.g., `C:\...` or `B:\...`) — they are not supported

### Virtual Path Routes

The filesystem backend routes paths to different directories:

| Virtual Path | Maps To | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | Project workspace root | Source code, config files |
| `/memories/` | `~/.nova/{agent-id}/` | User memory (agent.md, preferences) |
| `/project-memory/` | `{workspace}/.nova/` | Project memory (NOVA.md, CLAUDE.md) |
| `/.nova/plans/` | `{workspace}/.nova/plans/` | Plan files (plan-*.md) |
| `/skills/` | `~/.nova/skills/` | Global skills |

**Examples:**
- Read user memory: `read_file(path="/memories/agent.md")`
- Write project memory: `write_file(path="/project-memory/NOVA.md", content="...")`
- Write a plan: `write_file(path="/.nova/plans/plan-refactor.md", content="...")`
- Read a skill: `read_file(path="/skills/web-research/SKILL.md")`

